England might be almost ready to take their spot at Euro 2016, but the manager, Roy Hodgson, still does not know his best starting team.

Reports from the newspaper Sportsmail asked eleven players to pick their favorite line-up for the final match in France. They picked teams assuming all players are fit. You can show your ideal England team by posting them in the comments section below.

The suggested line-out was:

Hart;
Clyne, Cahill, Jagielka, Baines;
Henderson, Wilshere;
Welbeck, Rooney, Sterling;
Kane.

Roy Hodgson was pictured at the Juventus Stadium during a friendly match against Italy.
